<title>SINGAPORE: Malaysia lowers term price of Tapis crude $1.16.</title>
<headline>Malaysia lowers term price of Tapis crude $1.16.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian state-oil company Petronas has cut its April-lifting benchmark Tapis crude oil price to $21.23 per barrel, down $1.16 from $22.39 in March, traders said on Friday.  </p>
<p>For May, Petronas has set a premium of 30 cents per barrel for term crude oil sales of Tapis, down from 55 cents for April.</p>
<p>Labuan was set at a fixed differential of Tapis plus 15 cents and Miri was set at Tapis plus 10 cents.</p>
<p>Bintulu differential was set at Tapis less 40 cents.</p>
<p>The price of April Dulang crude was set at $20.35 per barrel, down $1.06 from $21.41 per barrel for March.</p>
<p>PETRONAS 1996/1997 TERM PRICES (INCLUDES ALPHA ADJUSTMENT)</p>
<p>	    APR     MAR     FEB     JAN     DEC     NOV     OCT</p>
<p>TAPIS   $21.23   $22.39  $23.79  $26.23  $25.44  $25.06  $25.70</p>
<p>LABUAN  $21.38   $22.54  $23.94  $26.38  $25.54  $25.16  $25.80</p>
<p>MIRI    $21.33   $22.49  $23.89  $26.33  $25.34  $25.01  $25.60</p>
<p>DULANG  $20.35   $21.41  $23.08  $25.66  $24.55  $24.10  $24.69</p>
<p>BINTULU $20.83   $21.89  $23.39  $25.83  $25.14  $24.76  $25.40</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
